.TH EXTENSIONS 1 "September 2026" "ProwseTk" "Prowse-TUI Help"
.SH NAME
extensions \- configure Lua extensions and native plugins
.SH LUA
Add a file with :config add-lua PATH and save. On the next launch each file
runs in the browser Lua runtime, in array order, after binding global session.
The script may install callbacks or manipulate the visible session.
A script is not automatically called as a driver main function.
.nf
local doc = session:document()
session:set_header("X-Automation", "prowse-tui")
.fi
.SH NATIVE PLUGINS
Add a native shared library with :config add-plugin PATH and save.
At startup PluginRegistry validates the native ABI, initializes plugins and
configures them before Lua extensions run. Session hooks remain host-mediated.
Only native plugin paths are accepted by this setting; WASM is not enabled.
.SH PATHS AND FAILURES
Relative paths resolve beside ProwseTUI.toml, not the working directory.
Paths containing spaces are accepted verbatim after the command name; do not
add shell quotes in :config commands. TOML strings use normal TOML quoting.
Each array permits at most 64 unique paths. Only add trusted local code:
Lua and native extensions execute with the application's privileges.
A load failure is reported without printing script contents or credentials.
Earlier extensions may already have run. Correct the configuration and restart.
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR config 1
.MR commands 1
